values
  ('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'nyll-art6', 'NYLL', 'NY Labor Law Article 6', array['Article 6'],
   'Payment of wages (sections 190 to 199 A): pay frequency, deductions, wage notices and statements, and wage claim remedies.',
   'Overtime. New York overtime is set by the wage orders under Article 19 (12 NYCRR 142 2.2).', array['overtime'], array['not', 'Article 19'], 'https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/LAB/A6'),
  ('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'nyll-art19', 'NYLL', 'NY Labor Law Article 19', array['Article 19'],
   'Minimum Wage Act (sections 650 to 665), under which the wage orders set minimum wage and overtime.',
   null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/LAB/A19'),
  ('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'nyll-191', 'NYLL', 'NY Labor Law § 191', array['191'],
   'How often wages must be paid: manual workers weekly (not later than 7 days after the week ends); clerical and other workers at least twice a month; commissioned salespersons under a written agreement.',
   'Overtime or minimum wage amounts.', array['overtime rate', 'minimum wage rate', 'time and a half'], '{}'::text[], 'https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/LAB/191'),
  ('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'nyll-193', 'NYLL', 'NY Labor Law § 193', array['193'],
   'Bars deductions from wages except those required by law or expressly authorized in writing by the employee for the employee''s benefit in the categories the law lists (for example insurance, pension, union dues).',
   'That uniform, cash shortage, breakage or walkout deductions are allowed with written consent. They are not.', array['uniform', 'cash shortage', 'breakage', 'walkout'], array['not', 'prohibit', 'bar', 'cannot', 'may not', 'even if', 'even with'], 'https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/LAB/193'),
  ('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'nyll-195', 'NYLL', 'NY Labor Law § 195', array['195', '195(1)', '195(3)', '195(4)'],
   'Employer notice and records: wage notice at hire (195(1)); wage statement with every payment (195(3)); keep payroll records for six years (195(4)).',
   'A right for private employees to inspect their personnel file.', array['personnel file'], array['no right', 'not give', 'does not', 'no general'], 'https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/LAB/195'),
  ('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'nyll-196b', 'NYLL', 'NY Labor Law § 196 b', array['196-b', '196(b)'],
   'New York State paid sick leave: 1 hour per 30 hours worked; up to 40 or 56 hours a year depending on employer size; paid or unpaid for the smallest employers depending on net income.',
   'New York City safe and sick time (that is NYC Admin. Code § 20 911 and following).', array['Earned Safe and Sick Time', 'safe and sick time'], array['separate', 'not', 'also'], 'https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/LAB/196-B'),
  ('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'nyll-196d', 'NYLL', 'NY Labor Law § 196 d', array['196-d', '196(d)'],
   'Gratuities: an employer or its agents (including managers) may not demand, accept or keep any part of an employee''s tips.',
   'The tip credit (that is in 12 NYCRR Part 146).', array['tip credit'], array['not the tip credit', 'separate', 'Part 146'], 'https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/LAB/196-D'),
  ('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'nyll-198', 'NYLL', 'NY Labor Law § 198', array['198', '198(1-a)', '198(1-b)', '198(1-d)', '198(3)'],
   'Remedies for wage claims: unpaid wages, liquidated damages of 100 percent, prejudgment interest; wage notice damages of $50 per workday up to $5,000 (198(1 b)); wage statement damages of $250 per workday up to $5,000 (198(1 d)); six year limitations period (198(3)).',
   '"$250 per violation"; that remedies are only available in a lawsuit.', array['per violation', 'only available through a lawsuit', 'only through a lawsuit', 'only in a lawsuit'], '{}'::text[], 'https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/LAB/198'),
  ('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'nyll-198c', 'NYLL', 'NY Labor Law § 198 c', array['198-c', '198(c)'],
   'Benefits and wage supplements (for example vacation pay, holiday pay, reimbursements): failure to pay within 30 days after they are due is a misdemeanor; does not apply to executive, administrative or professional employees earning over $1,300 a week.',
   'Any rule about waiving wage claims or releases.', array['waive', 'waiver', 'release'], array['does not', 'not about', 'nothing to do'], 'https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/LAB/198-C'),
  ('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'nyll-215', 'NYLL', 'NY Labor Law § 215', array['215'],
